// GPU class: high-texture-4096 — a control, and not a real device
//
// States a texture edge of 4096 voxels and 32 GB of texture memory. No known
// WebGL device holds an edge above 2048, so a deployment must not state this
// profile in production. Cornerstone3D marks the profile `internal`.
//
// The profile is the control of the demonstration. A series of up to 4096
// images renders with no reduction here, and the same series reduces under
// `gpu/high`. The pair shows that the reduction comes from the limit of the
// device and not from a defect.
//
// A real device rejects a texture of this edge, so the viewport can fail to
// allocate. That failure is the expected result on hardware, and it is the
// reason the profile is a control only.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/high-texture-4096`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuCapabilityProfile": "high-texture-4096"
  }
}
